  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "search_valid_dns",
    "file": "ndpi/src/lib/protocols/dns.c",
    "description": "In DNS reply parsing, `search_valid_dns` performs an unconditional `x++` (after header parsing) and then immediately reads `flow->packet.payload[x]` at line 144 without first checking that `x < payload_packet_len`. This creates an off-by-one out-of-bounds read when `x` is already at the last valid index after `x += sizeof(ndpi_dns_packet_header)` (plus payload_offset), so the subsequent access dereferences one byte past the heap buffer.",
    "conditions": "Input must be routed to DNS dissector (`ndpi_search_dns`) via UDP/TCP DNS ports and satisfy the initial length gate (`payload_packet_len > sizeof(dns_header)+payload_offset`) and reply-shape checks in `search_valid_dns` (flags indicate response and query/answer counters pass constraints). A crafted short/truncated DNS-reply-like payload can make `x` reach the end, then the unconditional increment/read path (`x++; if(payload[x] != '\\0')`) triggers the 1-byte heap OOB read. In the provided PoV, fuzzed packet bytes through `ndpi_detection_process_packet` -> `check_ndpi_udp_flow_func` -> `ndpi_search_dns` reach this path and crash at dns.c:144."
  },
